{"toolCallId":"call_6eaf5f8adecc41df9d1d13ef099900f5","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/acceptance-criteria.md:66:| AC-013 | REQ-009 | Given a run that writes a warning to stderr, When the script runs with `--quiet`, Then the warning still appears on stderr and stdout holds only the single level line | Capture stdout and stderr separately in `test-recommend-level-quiet.sh`; assert the warning text is in the stderr capture and stdout is one line | Unmet | - |\nspecs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/spec.md:100:| REQ-009 | With `--quiet`, any warning the script writes to stderr is still written to stderr, so `--quiet` trims stdout only |\nspecs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/tasks.md:59:- [ ] T023 Keep every warning the script writes to stderr on stderr in quiet mode, so `--quiet` trims stdout only, per REQ-009 (`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh`)\n"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/cwd":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w4fbf614733/tree","terminal_exit":{"terminal_id":"a3a485","exit_code":0,"signal":null},"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
